{#
  ICON — the single source for inline SVG.

  Every glyph in the site is defined once in the `paths` map below and rendered
  through this macro. Nothing else in the codebase should paste raw <svg> markup:
  the old index.html shipped the same 700-byte chevron five separate times, and
  every one of them had to be edited by hand to change a colour.

  PROPS
    name    key in the map below (required)
    size    px, applied to width AND height (default 24)
    rotate  degrees, for reusing one glyph in several directions (default 0)
    class   extra classes on the <svg>
    title   accessible name; when omitted the icon is aria-hidden (decorative)

  USAGE
    {% raw %}{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}
    {{ icon("chevron-down") }}
    {{ icon("chevron-down", rotate=90, title="Next project") }}{% endraw %}
#}

{#
  THE WORDMARK is in this map rather than an <img>, and that is load-bearing.
  The header flips between a light and a dark variant (Figma 446:37196), so
  the mark has to recolour with it — and an <img> cannot: SVG loaded that way
  is an isolated document that the page's CSS and `currentColor` never reach.
  Inline, it inherits `color` from .site-header__logo like every other glyph.

  Assets/images/hero/logo-mark.svg is the same artwork with fill="black" baked
  in. It is still what the OG/social tags point at, where a fixed colour is
  correct, so that file stays.
#}
